<p>The United States has designated Afghanistan a “State Sponsor of Wrongful Detention,” accusing the Taliban of holding Americans and other foreign nationals as leverage—what U.S. officials described as “hostage diplomacy”. Secretary of State Marco Rubio said the move reflects concerns about “unjust” detentions and warned that Afghanistan is not safe for Americans to visit. The designation gives the Trump administration another tool it can use to weigh penalties, including sanctions and export controls. At the same time, U.S. officials at the United Nations urged a fresh look at international engagement and aid mechanisms tied to Afghanistan, arguing that assistance should be measured against Taliban behavior and cooperation. Even with pressure rising, the U.S. message also keeps a practical focus: getting detained Americans home. Rubio called for the immediate release of U.S. nationals held in Afghanistan and for an end to the practice altogether.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_ygl9duF1Hzvy2zMtSEt5tCSsshxMzadQvhcSJim0BKhNImKLklhxVhNrQQDz4oQMXtioMot-rcO5hmEOnXnp0xWkANZin2kkrfSGeMe94b0' alt='US Secretary of State Marco Rubio speaks at the State Department in Washington, DC (file image).' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Named detainees: Rubio publicly urged the Taliban to release Dennis Coyle and Mahmoud Habibi, along with “all Americans unjustly detained in Afghanistan”.</li><li>Rubio’s language: He accused the Taliban of using “terrorist tactics,” including kidnapping people for ransom or to seek policy concessions, and said these “despicable tactics” “need to end”.</li><li>Possible travel limits: U.S. officials said the censure could lead to a ban on U.S. passport holders traveling to Afghanistan, adding to existing warnings to avoid travel there.</li><li>Related designation: The Hindu reported Iran received the same “wrongful detention” designation in February 2026—one day before the U.S. and Israel launched strikes against the Islamic Republic—putting Afghanistan within a broader U.S. pressure campaign against hostage-taking practices.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US State Department: Rubio said the Taliban “continues to unjustly detain our fellow Americans and other foreign nationals,” and urged the immediate release of U.S. nationals held in Afghanistan. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980478/us-designates-afghanistan-state-sponsor-of-wrongful-detention'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Trump administration (policy tools): CBS reported the designation can pave the way for penalties such as sanctions and export controls under the Trump administration. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-designates-afghanistan-state-sponsor-wrongful-detention/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>US mission to the UN: At the UN Security Council, Ambassador Mike Waltz questioned continued international engagement and funding for Afghanistan, and pointed to UNAMA’s scale—still the largest UN special political mission even after a 15% 2026 budget reduction—as a reason to reassess how international assistance is handled. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-us-accuses-taliban-of-hostage-diplomacy/a-76284731'>DW</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-us-accuses-taliban-of-hostage-diplomacy/a-76284731'>Afghanistan: US accuses Taliban of &#x27;hostage diplomacy&#x27;</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-designates-afghanistan-state-sponsor-wrongful-detention/'>U.S. designates Afghanistan as a state sponsor of wrongful detention</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-designates-afghanistan-as-a-sponsor-of-wrongful-detention-accuses-it-of-hostage-diplomacy/article70724889.ece'>U.S. designates Afghanistan as a sponsor of wrongful detention, accuses it of ’hostage diplomacy’</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/us-weighs-censuring-afghanistan-over-detained-americans-could-ban-us-travel-to-the-country'>US censures Afghanistan over detained Americans, could ban US travel to the country</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980478/us-designates-afghanistan-state-sponsor-of-wrongful-detention'>US designates Afghanistan ‘State Sponsor of Wrongful Detention’</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-adds-afghanistan-to-wrongful-detention-list-over-taliban-hostage-diplomacy-11192976#publisher=newsstand'>US Adds Afghanistan To Wrongful Detention List Over Taliban Hostage Diplomacy</a> - ndtv.com</li></ul>